  "title": "Occurrence, Preparation, and Properties of Transition Metals Summary",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "d2xrdev4jz1gqt0",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "761840132",
            "type": "h2"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The transition metals are elements with partially filled "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": " orbitals, located in the "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "d"
              },
              {
                "text": "-block of the periodic table. The reactivity of the transition elements varies widely from very active metals such as scandium and iron to almost inert elements, such as the platinum family of metals. The type of chemistry used in the isolation of the elements from their ores depends on the concentration of the element in its ore and the difficulty of reducing ions of the elements to the metals. Metals that are more reactive are more difficult to reduce."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3099226058",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Transition metals exhibit chemical behavior typical of metals. For example, they oxidize in air upon heating and react with elemental halogens to form halides. Elements that lie above hydrogen in the activity series react with acids, producing salts and hydrogen gas. Oxides, hydroxides, and carbonates of transition metal compounds in low oxidation states are basic. Halides and other salts are generally stable in water, although oxygen must be excluded in some cases. Most transition metals form a variety of stable oxidation states, allowing them to demonstrate a wide range of chemical reactivity."
              }
            ],
            "id": "3109137731",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "czj0lmgeor7z4z6",
